<tr>
    )
    ===========================================================================
    Defines a row in a table. Variables: - `tr_content`: The content inside the
</tr>

<tr>
    element, typically table cells (
    <td>or</td>
    <th>
        ). Defaults to a single default cell. - `tr_class`: The class attribute
        for the
        <tr>
            element. Defaults to "default-class". - `tr_id`: The id attribute
            for the
        </tr>
        <tr>
            element. Defaults to "default-id". - `tr_style`: The style
            attribute for the
        </tr>
        <tr>
            element. Defaults to "". Notes: - The `| safe` filter is used to
            include HTML content safely. - The
        </tr>

        <tr>
            element is used to define a row in an HTML table. Links: -
            https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/tr -
            https://www.w3schools.com/tags/tag_tr.asp #}
        </tr>

        <tr
            class="{{ tr_class | default('default-class') | e }}"
            id="{{ tr_id | default('default-id') | e }}"
            style="{{ tr_style | default('') | e }}"
        >
            {{ tr_content | default('
            <td>Default cell content</td>
            ') | safe }}
        </tr>
    </th>
</tr>
